    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: Student Organization & Work-Based Learning (S0-U3)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nUNIT OBJECTIVE: Students can explain DECA's purposes and structure, demonstrate leadership through participation, and identify the WBL opportunities available in this program.\nPLANNED WORK PRODUCT: WBL intake document per student + DECA membership enrollment + division role charter (8177 management students draft their own; 8175 marketing students receive rotation schedule)\nCOURSE ROLE: This is the moment the class becomes a business. Role assignments happen here. The General Manager is identified. Division structures are announced.\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-31, 8175-32, 8175-33, 8175-34, 8175-35, 8175-36, 8175-37, 8175-38\n\nCRITERIA\n\nCriterion 1: Addressing Elements of Student Life\n- 8175-31 Identify the purposes and goals of the student organization.\n    * Evidence of Identification of the purposes of the student organization should include\n    * Evidence of Identification of the goals of the student organization should include\n- 8175-32 Explain the benefits and responsibilities of membership in the student organization as a student and in professional/civic organizations as an adult.\n    * Evidence of Explanation of benefits should include\n    * Evidence of Explanation of responsibilities should include\n- 8175-34 Identify Internet safety issues and procedures for complying with acceptable use standards.\n    * Evidence of Identification should include the following:\n\nCriterion 2: Exploring Career and Technical Student Organizations\n- 8175-33 Demonstrate leadership skills through participation in student organization activities, such as meetings, programs, and projects.\n    * Evidence of participating in student organization activities including meetings, programs, and projects\n    * Evidence of demonstrating leadership roles within student organization settings\n    * Evidence of applying career and technical skills in competitive events and activities\n    * Evidence of collaborating with peers to plan and execute organization projects\n\nCriterion 3: Exploring Work-Based Learning\n- 8175-35 Identify the types of work-based learning (WBL) opportunities.\n    * Evidence of job shadowing\n    * Evidence of mentorship\n    * Evidence of externship\n    * Evidence of school-based enterprise\n    * Evidence of entrepreneurship\n    * Evidence of internship\n    * Evidence of service learning\n    * Evidence of clinical experience\n    * Evidence of cooperative education\n    * Evidence of Youth Registered Apprenticeship\n    * Evidence of Registered Apprenticeship\n    * Evidence of Supervised Agricultural Experience\n- 8175-36 (Optional) Reflect on lessons learned during the WBL experience.\n    * Evidence of workplace procedures\n    * Evidence of application of course competencies to WBL experience\n    * Evidence of new knowledge gained through the WBL experience\n- 8175-37 Explore career opportunities related to the WBL experience.\n    * Evidence of listing possible careers related to this course\n    * Evidence of describing each career\n    * Evidence of determining the education and experience required\n    * Evidence of exploring job opportunities, salaries, and benefits\n- 8175-38 (Optional) Participate in a WBL experience, when appropriate.\n    * Evidence of an emphasis on the relationship between course competencies and the WBL experience\n    * Evidence of adherence to workplace expectations during the WBL experience\n    * Evidence of completion of the WBL experience\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when the planned work product shows evidence for every competency listed above, in the student's own words, applied to the class conglomerate (its divisions, school store, events and esports program) or a real organization in sports, entertainment or events, and uses the unit vocabulary accurately (DECA, Work-based learning (WBL), Role charter, Acceptable use, Cooperative education). Each criterion needs specific examples, not general statements. Work that restates definitions without applying them, or leaves any listed competency without evidence, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Student Organization & Work-Based Learning (S0-U3)\n\nStudents can explain DECA's purposes and structure, demonstrate leadership through participation, and identify the WBL opportunities available in this program.\n\nWhat you will make: WBL intake document per student + DECA membership enrollment + division role charter (8177 management students draft their own; 8175 marketing students receive rotation schedule)\n\nYour role: This is the moment the class becomes a business. Role assignments happen here. The General Manager is identified. Division structures are announced.\n\nThe work: Students receive their division role assignment (or rotation schedule) and complete a WBL intake document: what is my role, what will I produce, how will I be evaluated, and how does my work connect to the conglomerate's goals?\n\nGo deeper:\n\n- DECA competitive events that align with marketing rotation tracks — which events match Creative Studio work, which match Promotions, which match Sales?\n- Career exploration (Task 37) in the context of marketing roles: what jobs exist in creative, promotions, and sales in sports and entertainment?\n\nYour work must show evidence of each of these:\n\n- Identify the purposes and goals of the student organization.\n- Explain the benefits and responsibilities of membership in the student organization as a student and in professional/civic organizations as an adult.\n- Identify Internet safety issues and procedures for complying with acceptable use standards.\n- Demonstrate leadership skills through participation in student organization activities, such as meetings, programs, and projects.\n- Identify the types of work-based learning (WBL) opportunities.\n- (Optional) Reflect on lessons learned during the WBL experience.\n- Explore career opportunities related to the WBL experience.\n- (Optional) Participate in a WBL experience, when appropriate.\n\nUse these terms accurately: DECA, Work-based learning (WBL), Role charter, Acceptable use, Cooperative education.\n\nWrite your response in the response zone below."
