    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: Digital Media & E-Commerce (S6-U1)\nCOURSE: 8177 Sports Entertainment and Event Management\nUNIT OBJECTIVE: Students can identify how e-commerce and digital transactions affect sports, entertainment, and event businesses.\nPLANNED WORK PRODUCT: Three deliverables: (1) Platform strategy document — which platforms the conglomerate operates, which audience segment each serves, who owns each channel, and what the posting cadence is. Based on Stage 3 market research data. (2) Four-week content calendar — planned posts across all active platforms, including match coverage schedule, store promotion posts, and event announcements. (3) Digital order intake process — a simple form or link that allows custom order inquiries outside of school hours, connected to the Store Manager's workflow.\nCOURSE ROLE: Store Manager develops the digital order intake process and connects it to the POS workflow. General Manager reviews the platform strategy for alignment with the conglomerate's brand and ethical standards from Stage 5. Esports Division / League Manager builds and administers the Discord server for the school community league, establishing channel structure, moderation rules, and posting permissions.\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8177-47\n\nCRITERIA\n\nCriterion 1: Exploring Sports, Entertainment, and Event Management\n- 8177-47 Identify how e-commerce and digital transactions affect sports, entertainment, and event businesses.\n    * Evidence of lodging and travel\n    * Evidence of retail stores sites\n    * Evidence of auction sites\n    * Evidence of ticket sales\n    * Evidence of merchandise development websites\n    * Evidence of mobile apps\n    * Evidence of secure payment methods\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when the planned work product shows evidence for every competency listed above, in the student's own words, applied to the class conglomerate (its divisions, school store, events and esports program) or a real organization in sports, entertainment or events, and uses the unit vocabulary accurately (Distribution channel, Content calendar, Conversion, Engagement, E-commerce, Streaming, Discord). Each criterion needs specific examples, not general statements. Work that restates definitions without applying them, or leaves any listed competency without evidence, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Digital Media & E-Commerce (S6-U1)\n\nStudents can identify how e-commerce and digital transactions affect sports, entertainment, and event businesses.\n\nWhat you will make: Three deliverables: (1) Platform strategy document — which platforms the conglomerate operates, which audience segment each serves, who owns each channel, and what the posting cadence is. Based on Stage 3 market research data. (2) Four-week content calendar — planned posts across all active platforms, including match coverage schedule, store promotion posts, and event announcements. (3) Digital order intake process — a simple form or link that allows custom order inquiries outside of school hours, connected to the Store Manager's workflow.\n\nYour role: Store Manager develops the digital order intake process and connects it to the POS workflow. General Manager reviews the platform strategy for alignment with the conglomerate's brand and ethical standards from Stage 5. Esports Division / League Manager builds and administers the Discord server for the school community league, establishing channel structure, moderation rules, and posting permissions.\n\nThe work: Students audit the conglomerate's current digital footprint, build a platform strategy using market research data, establish a content calendar for the next four weeks, and connect the school store's POS to a simple digital order intake process. The large format printer produces a digital channel map — which platform serves which audience segment — for classroom display.\n\nGo deeper:\n\n- E-commerce operations deep dive (Task 47): management students map the full digital transaction lifecycle for a custom order — from inquiry form submission through payment, production scheduling, fulfillment, and follow-up. They identify every point where a delay or error could occur and document the contingency for each.\n- Digital security and data handling: the order intake form collects student names and contact information. Management students draft a simple data handling policy — what information is collected, how it is stored, who has access, and how it is disposed of. This connects to Task 16 (information security) from Stage 0.\n- Cash flow implications of e-commerce: if the digital order intake process accepts payment at order submission, the conglomerate receives revenue before producing the item. Students calculate the cash flow advantage of this model vs. pay-at-pickup, and identify the risk if an order cannot be fulfilled.\n\nYour work must show evidence of each of these:\n\n- Identify how e-commerce and digital transactions affect sports, entertainment, and event businesses.\n\nUse these terms accurately: Distribution channel, Content calendar, Conversion, Engagement, E-commerce, Streaming, Discord.\n\nWrite your response in the response zone below."
